00:38:49,470 --> 00:38:51,236
CALLER ID BLOCKED

557
00:38:56,636 --> 00:38:57,636
Mother.

558
00:38:58,836 --> 00:39:00,106
These guys are for real.

559
00:39:00,470 --> 00:39:01,870
They're not ordinary people.

560
00:39:05,188 --> 00:39:06,488
Did he say 3 billion won?

561
00:39:08,889 --> 00:39:09,851
Yes, Mother.

562
00:39:10,336 --> 00:39:14,469
Make it 1 billion won in cash

563
00:39:14,470 --> 00:39:16,536
and fill the rest with newspapers.

564
00:39:17,203 --> 00:39:18,803
Can't we do that?

565
00:39:19,570 --> 00:39:20,569
What?

566
00:39:20,570 --> 00:39:21,669
I mean,

567
00:39:21,670 --> 00:39:24,319
you see it all the time in movies.

568
00:39:25,636 --> 00:39:27,532
On top, they stack them

569
00:39:28,403 --> 00:39:29,836
with 10,000 won bills.

570
00:39:30,670 --> 00:39:33,970
It'd be hard to check, right?

571
00:39:35,603 --> 00:39:37,103
I don't think that's a good idea, Mother.

572
00:39:39,903 --> 00:39:41,303
We need to report this
to the police...

573
00:39:44,103 --> 00:39:46,008
If you provoke
guys like these,

574
00:39:47,429 --> 00:39:49,095
it could cost Yi-gyeong her life...

575
00:39:54,036 --> 00:39:55,328
Shouldn't saving Yi-gyeong

576
00:39:56,036 --> 00:39:57,870
be our top priority, Mother-in-law?

577
00:40:08,103 --> 00:40:09,208
DIVORCE LAWYER HWANG MIN-JUNG

578
00:40:09,209 --> 00:40:10,242
Everyone does that.

579
00:40:12,423 --> 00:40:13,356
Pardon?

580
00:40:13,903 --> 00:40:15,902
I was checking, just in case.

581
00:40:15,903 --> 00:40:17,436
I'm not getting divorced right now.

582
00:40:18,203 --> 00:40:19,370
You're thinking this way, right?

583
00:40:20,503 --> 00:40:21,570
Well...

584
00:40:23,203 --> 00:40:24,536
That's how it starts.

585
00:40:26,582 --> 00:40:27,616
You're a housewife, right?

586
00:40:28,936 --> 00:40:29,769
Yes.

587
00:40:29,770 --> 00:40:30,670
And your daughter?

588
00:40:31,235 --> 00:40:32,490
She's going to college soon.

589
00:40:33,010 --> 00:40:34,310
You need to make a living.

590
00:40:35,570 --> 00:40:36,436
Pardon?

591
00:40:37,036 --> 00:40:40,236
You need to figure out
what you can take before the divorce.

592
00:40:50,803 --> 00:40:51,902
Here is your risotto.

593
00:40:51,903 --> 00:40:52,702
- Wow, that looks good.
- Thank you.

594
00:40:52,703 --> 00:40:53,836
Enjoy your meal.

595
00:40:56,103 --> 00:40:57,602
You like risotto, right?

596
00:40:57,603 --> 00:40:59,469
I'm saying this
as if you're like my niece.

597
00:40:59,470 --> 00:41:01,136
Don't let
your emotions take over.

598
00:41:02,103 --> 00:41:03,970
First, we need to get
an accurate assessment of assets.

599
00:41:04,503 --> 00:41:06,736
Even better if the husband’s at fault.

600
00:41:17,336 --> 00:41:19,802
Seyoon Building.

601
00:41:19,803 --> 00:41:21,236
52 SEJEONG-RO, YONGDAEMUN-GU, SEOUL

602
00:41:25,070 --> 00:41:28,636
Seyoon Building public value: 2.4 billion
Debt: 1.2 billion, Bank loan: 1 billion

603
00:41:31,170 --> 00:41:32,703
There's nothing left after the debts.

604
00:41:36,136 --> 00:41:37,803
I'm a woman in my late 40s,
and had my career interrupted

605
00:41:40,970 --> 00:41:43,803
It's true that you will be less in demand
in the job market

606
00:41:47,636 --> 00:41:49,136
Please think about it one more time.
Reality isn't like a drama

607
00:42:18,903 --> 00:42:20,602
Who’s at fault?

608
00:42:20,603 --> 00:42:24,403
Like cheating or something.

609
00:42:36,636 --> 00:42:39,203
Hey, you're pretty good.

610
00:42:40,770 --> 00:42:43,238
Now, you just have to meet
and do the exchange.

611
00:42:43,670 --> 00:42:45,135
I'll bring the money,

612
00:42:45,136 --> 00:42:47,281
so just make sure
you bring Yi-gyeong, okay?

613
00:42:48,236 --> 00:42:49,969
So, from now on,

614
00:42:49,970 --> 00:42:51,903
don't call me, okay?

615
00:42:52,436 --> 00:42:54,336
My mother-in-law
might come with me too.

616
00:42:55,570 --> 00:42:56,703
In that case,

617
00:42:57,170 --> 00:42:59,203
I should bring that mask along.

618
00:43:01,903 --> 00:43:02,870
Right,

619
00:43:03,736 --> 00:43:05,236
That's right.

620
00:43:05,703 --> 00:43:08,435
- You see, my mother-in-law knows you.
- Yeah.

621
00:43:08,436 --> 00:43:10,403
So don't come out
and even say anything.

622
00:43:10,770 --> 00:43:11,770
Got it?

623
00:43:12,336 --> 00:43:13,635
And then,

624
00:43:13,636 --> 00:43:15,040
park the car right there...

625
00:43:15,370 --> 00:43:16,753
Give me 1.5 billion.

626
00:43:17,136 --> 00:43:18,136
What?

627
00:43:20,936 --> 00:43:22,188
I said I wanted 1.5 billion.

628
00:43:26,570 --> 00:43:28,503
Hey, don't I deserve that much?

629
00:43:31,703 --> 00:43:33,803
SEOUL YONGDAEMUN POLICE STATION

630
00:43:42,270 --> 00:43:43,236
Ju-ran.

631
00:43:44,203 --> 00:43:46,613
I found the footage from the accident
involving Gyun. Want to see it?

632
00:43:47,029 --> 00:43:47,840
Really?

633
00:43:48,202 --> 00:43:49,235
Where was it?

634
00:43:49,236 --> 00:43:51,902
It was caught on a dashcam
from a motorcycle doing delivering nearby.

635
00:43:51,903 --> 00:43:55,679
It's a bit far, so it's hard to see.

636
00:44:00,903 --> 00:44:01,603
Wait a second.

637
00:44:02,603 --> 00:44:03,902
This person.

638
00:44:03,903 --> 00:44:04,903
Zoom in on this person.

639
00:44:09,003 --> 00:44:09,903
Isn't he

640
00:44:10,970 --> 00:44:12,603
Gyun's brother-in-law?

641
00:44:12,970 --> 00:44:15,015
It does look like him...

642
00:44:16,436 --> 00:44:17,363
Could it be?

643
00:44:19,370 --> 00:44:20,370
What are you guys doing?

644
00:44:20,936 --> 00:44:21,902
Sergeant Keum,

645
00:44:21,903 --> 00:44:25,015
we're checking Gyun's accident footage
and found something strange.

646
00:44:26,036 --> 00:44:27,543
- This person here...
- Hey.

647
00:44:28,476 --> 00:44:30,810
I know you're upset,
but it's just a hit-and-run.

648
00:44:31,603 --> 00:44:33,333
We've got the driver on the lookout.

649
00:44:34,836 --> 00:44:38,535
And about what I mentioned yesterday
about Jung Chang-su and Real Capital,

650
00:44:38,536 --> 00:44:40,135
the one Gyun was investigating...

651
00:44:40,136 --> 00:44:41,236
Cut that out!

652
00:44:41,570 --> 00:44:43,369
I told you to give it up,
didn't I?

653
00:44:43,370 --> 00:44:44,403
But the situation…

654
00:44:45,329 --> 00:44:48,120
Are you willing to take responsibility
if we mess with a foreign company?

655
00:44:49,107 --> 00:44:51,835
If you want to investigate,
bring back some evidence, okay?

656
00:44:51,836 --> 00:44:53,902
Hey, if I'm being honest,

657
00:44:53,903 --> 00:44:55,902
bring me Jung Chang-su's dead body
or something!

658
00:44:55,903 --> 00:44:57,403
- Sergeant Keum...
- Enough.

659
00:44:58,403 --> 00:45:00,435
A case just broke out. Get your stuff.

660
00:45:00,436 --> 00:45:02,070
What? All of a sudden?

661
00:45:02,303 --> 00:45:03,569
Oh, good timing. Come with me.

662
00:45:03,570 --> 00:45:04,469
Bo-ram!

663
00:45:04,470 --> 00:45:05,469
Follow me!

664
00:45:05,470 --> 00:45:06,702
Where are we going?

665
00:45:06,703 --> 00:45:09,136
Sir? You need to tell me.

666
00:46:00,383 --> 00:46:03,102
Oh, hello, Mr. Min.

667
00:46:03,103 --> 00:46:03,969
Hello.

668
00:46:03,970 --> 00:46:06,425
Hey, plant a bug for Mr. Min.

669
00:46:07,170 --> 00:46:08,402
- Hello.
- Hello.

670
00:46:08,403 --> 00:46:09,836
Could you take off your outerwear?

671
00:46:10,570 --> 00:46:13,302
- Your outerwear?
- Outerwear? Oh, right.

672
00:46:13,303 --> 00:46:14,836
- You can give that to me.
- Oh, here.

673
00:46:17,270 --> 00:46:20,136
It's for your safety,
so just bear with it a little.

674
00:46:20,570 --> 00:46:23,002
If you look here, there's a power button.

675
00:46:23,003 --> 00:46:24,102
Press the power button

676
00:46:24,103 --> 00:46:25,702
and you can turn it off when you're done.

677
00:46:25,703 --> 00:46:27,235
Make sure to keep it on
when going on site.

678
00:46:27,236 --> 00:46:28,402
We'll make sure you're safe.

679
00:46:28,403 --> 00:46:30,070
Could you put this in your ear?

680
00:46:30,970 --> 00:46:32,136
Don't be too nervous.

681
00:46:33,570 --> 00:46:35,147
- Hwal-sung.
- Yes?

682
00:46:35,603 --> 00:46:37,936
Don't grumble and just cooperate, okay?

683
00:46:38,203 --> 00:46:39,336
Yes, ma’am.

684
00:46:40,436 --> 00:46:41,503
Hmm...

685
00:46:43,870 --> 00:46:44,736
Here.

686
00:46:46,103 --> 00:46:47,569
You're all working hard.

687
00:46:47,570 --> 00:46:48,235
Yes.

688
00:46:53,570 --> 00:46:55,169
Why the police?

689
00:46:55,170 --> 00:46:56,936
I already explained enough.

690
00:46:58,803 --> 00:47:01,203
You want me to just
hand over 3 billion won?

691
00:47:04,636 --> 00:47:06,669
When the police
get involved in these matters,

692
00:47:07,149 --> 00:47:09,049
It’ll get very dangerous, ma’am.

693
00:47:11,703 --> 00:47:14,303
Better to leave it to the experts.

694
00:47:27,403 --> 00:47:28,870
Yes, are you ready?

695
00:47:37,636 --> 00:47:38,570
Got it.

696
00:48:08,836 --> 00:48:10,401
Let's get going, then.

697
00:48:10,402 --> 00:48:12,469
Team 1 will head out first and wait.

698
00:48:12,470 --> 00:48:14,169
Koh Ju-ran, Yoon Bo-ram, and I

699
00:48:14,170 --> 00:48:16,269
will follow Mr. Min, okay?

700
00:48:16,270 --> 00:48:17,736
Yes, sergeant.

701
00:48:22,103 --> 00:48:24,002
- Sir.
- Yes?

702
00:48:24,003 --> 00:48:24,970
You've been working hard.

703
00:48:27,503 --> 00:48:28,670
I'm counting on you.

704
00:48:30,203 --> 00:48:33,102
Oh, why all of a sudden?

705
00:48:33,103 --> 00:48:36,003
Ma'am, this is risky.
It's not like before.

706
00:48:36,949 --> 00:48:38,649
But can I go with you?

707
00:48:39,670 --> 00:48:40,770
With me?

708
00:48:42,403 --> 00:48:43,969
I can just

709
00:48:43,970 --> 00:48:45,248
ride in your car.

710
00:48:46,270 --> 00:48:47,669
But that's a bit

711
00:48:47,670 --> 00:48:49,036
dangerous.

712
00:48:50,336 --> 00:48:51,936
She's my daughter
and it's my money.

713
00:48:52,336 --> 00:48:54,570
I'll stay quietly in the car,
just so you know.

714
00:48:55,203 --> 00:48:56,869
Hmm,

715
00:48:56,870 --> 00:48:58,403
okay.

716
00:49:13,536 --> 00:49:14,769
Don't worry.

717
00:49:14,770 --> 00:49:16,136
We're here for you.

718
00:49:19,496 --> 00:49:21,496
I'm going to the bathroom.

719
00:49:37,889 --> 00:49:40,511
The police are all over.
Just don't come out.

720
00:49:50,170 --> 00:49:54,035
TPAAO

721
00:49:54,036 --> 00:49:56,202
If you want to be on time,
you need to leave now.

722
00:49:56,203 --> 00:49:57,069
Are you okay?

723
00:49:57,070 --> 00:49:57,903
Yes.

724
00:49:58,770 --> 00:50:00,594
I'll be right out.

725
00:51:26,170 --> 00:51:27,736
Huh? Damn it.

726
00:51:34,070 --> 00:51:35,170
Mr. Gi.

727
00:51:36,836 --> 00:51:39,036
Yes, Mr. Oh.

728
00:51:47,703 --> 00:51:49,979
If you needed help,
you could have asked me.

729
00:51:51,202 --> 00:51:52,802
I thought you would be busy.

730
00:51:52,803 --> 00:51:53,836
Gosh.

731
00:51:55,319 --> 00:51:56,935
Oh,

732
00:51:56,936 --> 00:51:57,900
why is this so heavy?

733
00:51:58,636 --> 00:52:00,602
It's just that

734
00:52:00,603 --> 00:52:02,436
I had some stuff left.

735
00:52:07,649 --> 00:52:08,582
Your brother-in-law's?

736
00:52:09,036 --> 00:52:10,670
Right.

737
00:52:11,170 --> 00:52:12,702
He left a lot of stuff.

738
00:52:12,703 --> 00:52:14,522
I should move it quickly.

739
00:52:14,870 --> 00:52:16,636
Hey, I'll do it.

740
00:52:17,803 --> 00:52:20,770
How were you supposed to carry this alone?

741
00:52:23,003 --> 00:52:24,969
This isn't working. I can't lift it.

742
00:52:24,970 --> 00:52:26,435
I'll push from behind.

743
00:52:26,436 --> 00:52:27,436
Okay.

744
00:52:27,970 --> 00:52:28,936
Be careful.

745
00:52:30,136 --> 00:52:31,303
Lift it up from below.

746
00:52:32,503 --> 00:52:34,070
This is too heavy for me.

747
00:52:38,470 --> 00:52:40,402
Okay, we're good now.

748
00:52:40,403 --> 00:52:41,902
- Drop it here.
- Right here?

749
00:52:41,903 --> 00:52:43,635
Yes, just leave it here, Mr. Oh.

750
00:52:43,636 --> 00:52:46,136
It's okay. Thank you.

751
00:52:47,103 --> 00:52:48,269
You can go in now, Mr. Oh.

752
00:52:48,270 --> 00:52:49,269
Thank you.

753
00:52:49,270 --> 00:52:50,347
By the way,

754
00:52:51,436 --> 00:52:52,267
I helped

755
00:52:54,203 --> 00:52:55,969
you move that.

756
00:52:55,970 --> 00:52:57,303
Could you help me out a bit too?

757
00:52:59,436 --> 00:53:00,369
What do you need?

758
00:53:02,170 --> 00:53:03,136
That one.

759
00:53:03,703 --> 00:53:05,136
Please help me move that plant.

760
00:53:08,936 --> 00:53:10,235
Oh, sure.

761
00:53:10,236 --> 00:53:11,435
Right now.

762
00:53:11,436 --> 00:53:12,970
- Sure.
- Yes.

763
00:53:21,170 --> 00:53:25,069
My mom traveled to Vietnam 20 years ago

764
00:53:25,070 --> 00:53:26,602
- and bought this seedling...
- Yes.

765
00:53:26,603 --> 00:53:28,535
Over there, not here.

766
00:53:28,536 --> 00:53:29,503
Over there.

767
00:53:31,036 --> 00:53:31,469
Yes.

768
00:53:31,470 --> 00:53:33,170
She bought this seedling.

769
00:53:33,470 --> 00:53:35,436
Okay, got it.

770
00:53:36,670 --> 00:53:39,335
She raised it with care for 20 years,

771
00:53:39,336 --> 00:53:40,835
then when she heard I opened a cafe,

772
00:53:40,836 --> 00:53:43,035
- she gave it to me.
- I see.

773
00:53:43,036 --> 00:53:46,669
It needs rain and has to grow naturally.

774
00:53:46,670 --> 00:53:48,569
What do you think?
It really suits the building, doesn't it?

775
00:53:48,570 --> 00:53:49,402
Yes.

776
00:53:49,403 --> 00:53:51,335
It looks really great together.

777
00:53:51,336 --> 00:53:53,670
- I need to get going.
- Oh, but did you know?

778
00:53:54,976 --> 00:53:55,743
About what?

779
00:53:56,149 --> 00:53:57,449
The bathroom is clogged again.

780
00:53:58,803 --> 00:54:00,036
Then, we have to fix it.

781
00:54:00,508 --> 00:54:01,808
When will you fix it?

782
00:54:04,903 --> 00:54:07,069
This weekend,
I'll make sure to take care of it, okay?

783
00:54:07,070 --> 00:54:08,470
- Really?
- Take care, Mr. Oh.

784
00:54:10,070 --> 00:54:11,436
Need help?

785
00:54:12,103 --> 00:54:13,103
No thanks.

786
00:54:19,036 --> 00:54:20,936
Did he buy a car without telling me?

787
00:54:29,503 --> 00:54:31,103
Driver, please follow that car.

788
00:54:42,436 --> 00:54:44,236
Once you leave, we'll follow you.

789
00:56:02,770 --> 00:56:03,836
Where is he going?

790
00:56:04,470 --> 00:56:06,236
Mr. Min, where are you headed?

791
00:56:06,892 --> 00:56:07,895
I'm sorry, but

792
00:56:07,896 --> 00:56:09,063
my stomach is hurting.

793
00:56:10,703 --> 00:56:11,769
Sergeant Keum,

794
00:56:11,770 --> 00:56:13,902
Mr. Min will stop
by the restroom first.

795
00:56:13,903 --> 00:56:15,035
You go on ahead.

796
00:56:15,036 --> 00:56:16,270
Okay, hurry up then.

797
00:56:39,303 --> 00:56:40,603
I'll be right back.

798
00:56:41,003 --> 00:56:42,635
I'll pull it out right now.

799
00:56:42,636 --> 00:56:45,372
I'll pull it out for just a moment.
I'm sorry.

800
00:57:19,736 --> 00:57:20,770
Damn it.

801
00:57:46,803 --> 00:57:49,303
Please use the front door
This is the back entrance

802
00:58:05,703 --> 00:58:06,903
What are you doing, sir?

803
00:58:10,603 --> 00:58:11,970
Is there a payphone here?

804
00:58:13,470 --> 00:58:14,928
What's a payphone?

805
00:58:16,403 --> 00:58:18,736
You know, the one
where you put in coins to make calls.

806
00:58:20,536 --> 00:58:22,036
Just use a cell phone.

807
00:58:24,236 --> 00:58:25,703
Let me use your cell phone.

808
00:58:26,036 --> 00:58:26,970
What?

809
00:58:36,303 --> 00:58:37,376
What is this?

810
00:58:40,303 --> 00:58:41,270
Damn it.

811
00:58:48,770 --> 00:58:51,103
Gosh, that scared me.

812
00:59:14,003 --> 00:59:15,303
Drop me off here.

813
00:59:34,836 --> 00:59:35,935
Huh?

814
00:59:35,936 --> 00:59:36,736
Is that the one?

815
00:59:42,803 --> 00:59:43,736
Hey, Captain Kang.

816
00:59:44,470 --> 00:59:46,203
When are Detective Ko and Mr. Min coming?

817
00:59:46,908 --> 00:59:48,241
Someone just came in.

818
00:59:48,242 --> 00:59:49,709
Yes, they're leaving soon.

819
00:59:49,710 --> 00:59:51,943
Okay, tell them to hurry.

820
00:59:54,170 --> 00:59:55,536
Damn, is that it?

821
00:59:58,370 --> 01:00:00,169
Hmm,

822
01:00:00,170 --> 01:00:01,070
that's it.

823
01:00:02,803 --> 01:00:04,136
- I think that's it.
- What?

824
01:00:15,336 --> 01:00:16,870
Let's do this.

825
01:00:32,070 --> 01:00:34,270
Damn, I can't see.

826
01:00:37,170 --> 01:00:38,829
What are you doing?

827
01:00:39,542 --> 01:00:40,808
What are you doing, Su-jong?

828
01:00:41,503 --> 01:00:43,335
I don't think
they're answering.

829
01:00:43,336 --> 01:00:44,570
Hmm...

830
01:00:46,170 --> 01:00:48,269
- Can I get my phone back?
- Text message.

831
01:00:48,270 --> 01:00:49,203
Text.

832
01:00:49,636 --> 01:00:51,470
- What?
- Hurry and set up texting.

833
01:00:52,703 --> 01:00:56,270
- What text?
- Hurry up. There's no time.

834
01:00:56,836 --> 01:00:58,070
Hurry up.

835
01:00:59,103 --> 01:01:00,036
Here you go.

836
01:01:05,436 --> 01:01:06,435
What is this?

837
01:01:06,436 --> 01:01:07,769
Damn, kid.

838
01:01:07,770 --> 01:01:08,402
You use the Cheonjiin layout?

839
01:01:08,403 --> 01:01:09,772
Hey, type it for me.

840
01:01:11,070 --> 01:01:12,236
Come on, do it for me.

841
01:01:12,903 --> 01:01:14,036
What should I type?

842
01:01:14,037 --> 01:01:15,619
"Cops are here. Run."

843
01:01:16,503 --> 01:01:17,242
What?

844
01:01:17,243 --> 01:01:19,347
No, it's not what you think.
Just type it.

845
01:01:20,302 --> 01:01:22,313
I think I'll be home late today.

846
01:01:23,670 --> 01:01:24,703
- Welcome.
- Hello.

847
01:01:26,203 --> 01:01:27,003
Yes.

848
01:01:28,870 --> 01:01:29,770
I mean, it's just that

849
01:01:31,870 --> 01:01:33,103
I'm going to meet the kidnapper.

850
01:01:33,770 --> 01:01:34,703
The suspect.

851
01:01:43,436 --> 01:01:44,636
Got it.

852
01:01:45,570 --> 01:01:46,536
Okay.

853
01:02:07,036 --> 01:02:08,370
That will be 5,400 won.

854
01:02:09,936 --> 01:02:11,103
Can I have a receipt?

855
01:02:23,003 --> 01:02:24,170
Thank you.

856
01:02:25,336 --> 01:02:26,336
Have a nice day.

857
01:02:26,936 --> 01:02:28,370
Have a nice day.

858
01:02:44,470 --> 01:02:47,770
What the heck is this?

859
01:02:54,270 --> 01:02:55,936
Damn, fingerprints.

860
01:03:27,070 --> 01:03:29,036
Why is this guy taking so long?

861
01:03:30,103 --> 01:03:33,202
Enter the parking lot slowly.

862
01:03:33,203 --> 01:03:35,770
We'll be hiding behind you,
so don't worry.

863
01:04:06,536 --> 01:04:08,235
Sergeant, this is Bo-ram.

864
01:04:08,236 --> 01:04:09,935
We've arrived at the scene.

865
01:04:12,642 --> 01:04:13,942
Is he here?

866
01:04:14,936 --> 01:04:16,236
Don't worry.

867
01:04:16,636 --> 01:04:18,169
Hey, Detective Go.

868
01:04:18,170 --> 01:04:20,436
Tell Mr. Min to move naturally.

869
01:04:22,536 --> 01:04:24,603
Don't be nervous
and just move comfortably.

870
01:04:36,103 --> 01:04:37,203
Hurry up!

871
01:04:41,470 --> 01:04:42,336
Police.

872
01:04:43,503 --> 01:04:44,803
What is he saying?

873
01:04:45,403 --> 01:04:46,870
Police.

874
01:04:49,536 --> 01:04:50,570
Police.

875
01:04:58,803 --> 01:04:59,870
A suspect has appeared.

876
01:05:00,370 --> 01:05:01,269
Police.

877
01:05:01,270 --> 01:05:02,235
What?

878
01:05:02,236 --> 01:05:03,469
What are you saying?

879
01:05:03,470 --> 01:05:04,936
Okay, okay!

880
01:05:08,903 --> 01:05:10,303
Okay, we're good?

881
01:05:11,270 --> 01:05:12,836
- Damn it.
- Move it.

882
01:05:13,436 --> 01:05:14,736
Give me back my wife.

883
01:05:15,736 --> 01:05:17,603
Load this up and give her back.

884
01:05:18,036 --> 01:05:19,269
- Okay.
- Why are you being so polite?

885
01:05:19,270 --> 01:05:20,827
Hey! Come on!

886
01:05:21,270 --> 01:05:23,369
Enough! I don't want to hear any of this!

887
01:05:23,370 --> 01:05:25,070
Now where's my wife?

888
01:05:27,136 --> 01:05:27,735
Are you acting too?

889
01:05:27,736 --> 01:05:30,602
My wife! Where is she?

890
01:05:30,603 --> 01:05:31,402
Is your mother-in-law here?

891
01:05:31,403 --> 01:05:32,635
Wife!

892
01:05:32,636 --> 01:05:33,502
Hurry up!

893
01:05:33,503 --> 01:05:34,403
Wife!

894
01:05:34,670 --> 01:05:36,702
- Where's my wife?
- You crazy bastard.

895
01:05:36,703 --> 01:05:37,602
I said where's my wife?

896
01:05:37,603 --> 01:05:38,902
She's in the trunk.

897
01:05:38,903 --> 01:05:41,074
Hey! Yi-gyeong!

898
01:05:41,903 --> 01:05:42,903
Ready to pounce.

899
01:05:50,636 --> 01:05:52,003
Secure the position and wait.

900
01:05:52,403 --> 01:05:53,735
- Hand it over.
- Wait.

901
01:05:53,736 --> 01:05:54,570
Hey...

902
01:05:58,636 --> 01:06:01,203
Ma'am, where are you going?
Don't do it!

903
01:06:01,736 --> 01:06:04,402
But we have to catch him now.

904
01:06:04,403 --> 01:06:05,670
What if he just runs off with the money?

905
01:06:08,870 --> 01:06:09,970
Damn it.

906
01:06:10,736 --> 01:06:11,770
Hey, what are you doing?

907
01:06:12,036 --> 01:06:12,970
Stop right there!

908
01:06:13,370 --> 01:06:14,736
Hurry up! Hurry up!

909
01:06:16,868 --> 01:06:18,970
Damn it!

910
01:06:19,970 --> 01:06:22,170
Let go of me!

911
01:06:24,303 --> 01:06:26,370
I'm sorry!

912
01:06:36,703 --> 01:06:37,603
Get him!

913
01:06:44,836 --> 01:06:45,936
Get him!

914
01:06:47,403 --> 01:06:48,436
Hey!

915
01:06:49,303 --> 01:06:50,103
Open the door!

916
01:06:50,470 --> 01:06:52,735
- Pull over!
- Open the door!

917
01:06:52,736 --> 01:06:53,570
Pull over!

918
01:06:54,170 --> 01:06:56,270
- Open the door!
- Pull over!

919
01:07:21,336 --> 01:07:24,370
MAD CONCRETE DREAMS

920
01:07:24,603 --> 01:07:26,169
Did you see the suspect's face?

921
01:07:26,170 --> 01:07:27,202
Why are your hands like this?

922
01:07:27,203 --> 01:07:28,435
It makes you look suspicious.

923
01:07:28,636 --> 01:07:30,469
You know what happened, right?

924
01:07:30,470 --> 01:07:31,669
Only the wife was kidnapped.

925
01:07:31,670 --> 01:07:32,802
What is this?

926
01:07:32,803 --> 01:07:33,735
A bag.

927
01:07:33,736 --> 01:07:34,602
A hiking bag.

928
01:07:34,603 --> 01:07:35,635
So I'm asking

929
01:07:35,636 --> 01:07:37,002
what's inside it?

930
01:07:37,003 --> 01:07:38,202
It's 3 billion won.

931
01:07:38,203 --> 01:07:41,535
That guy took 3 billion won
as your ransom.

932
01:07:41,536 --> 01:07:42,602
It's nice.

933
01:07:42,603 --> 01:07:44,602
Is this the guy
you saw last night?

934
01:07:44,603 --> 01:07:47,002
You're under arrest for robbery,
assault, and kidnapping.

935
01:07:47,003 --> 01:07:48,803
Let go! Let go of me!

936
01:07:49,170 --> 01:07:50,103
Let go!

